From: Neutron lab (team agent unsecapp) 2026-11-07
Subject: [PATCH] programs/unsecapp: Add the Unsecured Apartment local server (WMI async sink host).

What was seen (lab, Adobe Acrobat Pro 21.001.20135): from the second Acrobat launch on, Adobe's AGMService.exe (Adobe
Genuine Monitor Service, a 32-bit auto-start service installed with Acrobat) dies with a Wine "Program Error" dialog
on every launch (n=4 earlier rounds, n=2 here before the fix): page fault reading 0x0 at agmservice+0x56315.

Mechanism (+ole/+wbemprox/+seh trace and disassembly): the service thread does what Microsoft's sample "Receiving
event notifications through WMI" does: CoInitializeEx(MTA), WbemLocator -> ConnectServer("ROOT\CIMV2"),
CoSetProxyBlanket, then CoCreateInstance(CLSID_UnsecuredApartment {49bd2028-...}, CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER,
IID_IUnsecuredApartment). Wine has no such class (no unsecapp.exe, no registration): combase logs "class not
registered" and returns REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG (0x80040154, measured by the new test on the unpatched build). The
service does not check the result and calls CreateObjectStub through the NULL pointer. Next on its path:
QueryInterface(stub, IID_IWbemObjectSink), then IWbemServices::ExecNotificationQueryAsync("WQL",
"Select * From Win32_ProcessStartTrace Where processName=..." (a list of Adobe app executables),
WBEM_FLAG_SEND_STATUS, NULL, stub sink).

Windows behavior: unsecapp.exe (System32\wbem) is the COM local server for CLSID_UnsecuredApartment. Its
IUnsecuredApartment::CreateObjectStub / IWbemUnsecuredApartment::CreateSinkStub wrap a client's IWbemObjectSink
in a forwarder living in the unsecapp process; WMI calls Indicate/SetStatus on the forwarder, which passes them on
to the client's sink. The WMI interfaces it uses are marshalable across processes.

Fix:
- programs/unsecapp: the local server. MTA, REGCLS_MULTIPLEUSE; the apartment object exposes IUnsecuredApartment and
  IWbemUnsecuredApartment; both methods return a forwarder that implements IWbemObjectSink and forwards Indicate and
  SetStatus to the client's sink. The process exits when its last object is released. Like Wine's other background
  servers it marks itself a Wine system process, so it never keeps a prefix's session alive on its own (it exits
  with the session).
- wbemprox: proxy/stub code for the non-local interfaces of wbemcli.idl (IWbemObjectSink, IUnsecuredApartment,
  IWbemUnsecuredApartment, IWbemServices, IWbemCallResult, IEnumWbemClassObject, ...), registered by wbemprox's
  DllRegisterServer with PSFactoryBuffer {7c857801-...} (= IID_IWbemObjectSink). Windows hosts these proxies in its
  own WMI DLLs; which DLL is not modeled here.
- wine.inf: unsecapp.exe in system32\wbem (both arches), HKCR\CLSID\{49BD2028-...} AppID + LocalServer32 =
  %11%\wbem\unsecapp.exe, HKCR\AppID\{49BD2028-...} and HKCR\AppID\unsecapp.exe. A 32-bit client finds the 64-bit
  registration through combase's opposite-view lookup and starts the 64-bit server, as on 64-bit Windows.
- wbemprox tests: test_UnsecuredApartment (local server activation, CreateObjectStub + QI IWbemObjectSink,
  CreateSinkStub, SetStatus forwarded to the client's sink).

Not covered:
- No WMI event provider: Win32_ProcessStartTrace events are never delivered. Wine's ExecNotificationQueryAsync
  (unchanged) runs the query once as a data query and reports SetStatus(WBEM_STATUS_COMPLETE, S_OK) at once; AGMService
  logs "Process Creation Monitoring enabled..." and then idles.
- IWbemClassObject is a [local] interface (Windows marshals it by value with custom marshaling): Indicate() with
  objects through a forwarder fails to marshal under Wine. AGMService's path never calls Indicate.
- Wine has no DCOM ping rundown: a client that dies without releasing leaves its forwarder alive until the session
  ends (Windows releases it after the ping timeout).
- wineboot starts auto-start services before it applies wine.inf: on the first start after updating a prefix to a
  runtime with this patch (the wineboot -u boot), AGMService can run before the registration exists and crash once
  (seen 3 of 3 such boots); every later start is clean.
- widl also writes CLSID default-name keys for wbemcli.idl's other coclasses (WbemClassObject, WbemStatusCodeText,
  WbemRefresher; no server, so creating them still fails as before).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-185 + 185ao's riched20 + this patch = 11.10-185us; prefixes = reflinks of the lab's base
Acrobat install; nested KWin desk at 168 dpi):
  Acrobat launches, switch on: 4 of 4 clean (2 + 2 on two prefixes; 2 on the final build): no Program Error, AGMService
  running, unsecapp.exe running, AGMService's own log (adobegc.log) says "Process Creation Monitoring enabled...",
  Acrobat window up, Ctrl+Q quits Acrobat.
  Kill switch NEUTRON_UNSECAPP=0 (prefix registry environment, same build): 2 of 2 launches show the Program Error
  again, no unsecapp, no "Monitoring enabled" line.
  Session end: boot + exit of the only user process -> 0 processes 45 s later; unsecapp traced "session ending".
  Service stop (net stop AGMService): service stops; the forwarder stays (AGMService never cancels; see above).
  Wine's wbemprox tests (x64, 2 runs per arm): query 1647 tests 0 failures both arms; services 71 tests 1 failure
  (the new test: 0x80040154) unpatched, 81 tests 0 failures patched.
  Other Adobe apps: AGMService is not installed in the lab Creative Cloud prefixes (PgD-pr2/ps2/lrc2: no
  AdobeGCClient folder, no AGM service). Several CC binaries contain the CLSID bytes (dunamis-ingest.dll, IMSLib.dll,
  Registration.dll, ...), but none of 1928 lab CC launch logs shows an UnsecuredApartment activation.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_UNSECAPP=0 (read by unsecapp.exe from its environment, inherited from the client). Windows
services get a fresh environment block, so for a service client set it in the prefix's registry environment
(HKCU\Environment).
---
